    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 62 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation on `POST /api/owners`. When a request repeats with an already-seen `Idempotency-Key` header, the originally created owner is returned with 200 instead of creating a duplicate.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (no `@RestController`), I added:\n\n**New Spring bean** \u2014 `rest/idempotency/IdempotencyStore.java`: a process-wide `@Component` mapping each seen key \u2192 the owner id it created (survives across requests, injected into functions by type).\n\n**Two new pipeline functions** in `rest/function/owner/`:\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey` \u2014 new entry point. Reads the optional header via `@RequestHeader(required = false)`. If the key was seen before and its owner still exists, it loads that owner, publishes it, and takes the `existing` output branch (short-circuiting the pipeline). Otherwise it publishes the key and takes the `create` branch into the normal validate\u2192save pipeline.\n- `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 runs after `save` (so the id is assigned); records key \u2192 owner id when a key was present.\n\n**Wiring** in `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- `checkIdempotency` is now the first step, using `outputs: { existing: respondExisting, create: validate }` for the conditional branch (`@Flow`-based, per AGENTS.md).\n- `respondExisting` reuses the existing `RespondWithOwner` (200 responder).\n- `recordIdempotency` inserted between `save` and `audit`.\n\nAll new steps carry `govern: [ transaction ]`, consistent with the rest of the pipeline. Behavior is unchanged when no header is present (verified \u2014 full suite green: 62/62).",
