    "probe_text": "I now have the complete picture. Here is the ordered walkthrough of `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization:** the whole endpoint is guarded by `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request is denied (`AuthorizationDeniedException`) before the pipeline runs.\n\nEvery step below runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all reads/writes share one transaction that commits once at the very end.\n\n## Pipeline steps, in execution order\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`** *(side-effects + a branch, no validation)*\n- Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header and **publishes it** (even if null) for the later recording step.\n- If the key was seen before *and* its owner still exists: loads that owner, publishes it, and **short-circuits to `RespondWithOwner` (HTTP 200)** \u2014 none of the steps below run, nothing new is created.\n- Otherwise branches to `validate` to run the normal create pipeline.\n\n**2. `ValidateOwnerFields`** \u2014 the one step that binds `@RequestBody`. In order:\n- **Normalizes the address in place** (`OwnerAddress.normalize`): trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`; prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` and composes the flat `address`, else normalizes the flat `address`. (side-effect that feeds the next validation)\n- **Required-field validation:** rejects with `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400) listing every field that is null/blank among `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (the composed one), `city`, `telephone`.\n- **Telephone normalization + validation** (`OwnerTelephone.normalize`): strips separators, forces E.164 (assumes `+61`, drops one leading `0`), requires 8\u201315 digits, and for known country codes an exact national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Stores the E.164 form; invalid \u2192 `InvalidOwnerTelephoneException` (400).\n- **Email validation + normalization** (`OwnerEmail.normalize`): only when present/non-blank \u2014 syntax check, reject disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), store trimmed + lower-cased; invalid \u2192 `InvalidOwnerEmailException` (400).\n- **Postcode validation** (`OwnerPostcode.validate`): only when present \u2014 must be 4 digits and, if the city maps to a region, within that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); stores trimmed value; invalid \u2192 `InvalidOwnerPostcodeException` (400).\n- **Registration-date validation** (`OwnerRegistrationDate.validate`): only when present \u2014 the supplied date (checked as-is, pre-adjustment) must not be after the server date; future \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n- Publishes the validated DTO.\n\n**3. `BuildOwner`** \u2014 maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity, then **sets its registration date to the business-day-adjusted effective date** (`BusinessDay.effective`: supplied-or-today, rolling weekends and listed 2026 public holidays forward).\n\n**4. `AssignHousehold`** \u2014 **stamps `householdId`** = first 12 hex of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName|postcode)`. Deterministic; no validation.\n\n**5. `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`** \u2014 **household-duplicate check:** if `sharesHousehold` is true, skip. Otherwise scan all non-deleted owners; if any shares this `householdId`, reject with `HouseholdDuplicateException` (409).\n\n**6. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`** \u2014 **identity-duplicate check** (never bypassed): compute `identityKey` = `telephone|email|householdId`; if any non-deleted owner has the same key, reject with `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n\n**7. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** \u2014 reject if the owner's city (case-insensitive) already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n**8. `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`** \u2014 reject if \u2265 100 existing owners already carry this owner's effective business-day registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n\n**9. `AssignHouseholdSize`** \u2014 **sets `householdSize`** = count of existing owners sharing `householdId`, plus this one (1 when no household).\n\n**10. `AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 **sets `customerCode`** = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city, HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of `SHA-256(telephone+lastName)`); if it collides with an existing code, append `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 until unique.\n\n**11. `AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 **sets `namesakeCount`** = number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n**12. `AssignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 **sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`.** Defaults false/null. Skips (stays false) if `sharesHousehold` or if lastName/postcode/telephone is null. Otherwise flags true, pointing at the smallest-id non-deleted owner sharing lastName (case-insensitive) + postcode but with a *different* telephone.\n\n**13. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 **persists the owner** (assigns its id).\n\n**14. `RecordIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, **records key \u2192 saved owner id** in the `IdempotencyStore` so a later repeat replays this owner.\n\n**15. `AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 **emits an `AUDIT` log line** with id, customerCode, registrationDate, numeric membershipLevel, and a derived membershipNumber (`<customerCode>-M<fiscalYY>`).\n\n**16. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto`, **sets `bulkSignupWarning`** true when > 80 owners already share this registration day, and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes on ordering rationale\n- All field validation (400s) happens in step 2, *before* any lookup-based rejection, so a malformed body fails fast.\n- Duplicate/capacity/limit rejections (409/429) come after the entity and its `householdId` are finalized but before any derived counts are assigned and before save.\n- The `sharesHousehold` flag bypasses only the household-duplicate check (step 5) and the soft possible-duplicate flag (step 12) \u2014 never the identity check (step 6).\n\nAny exception thrown falls to its handler under `officefloor/escalation/`; the shared transaction rolls back rather than committing."
